rule: ELIM-G-2
The match on the known constructor Some is gone from the specialization.
CHECK: -- specialization of Main.apply(Main.Some(lam{{[0-9]+}}[]); _:Int)
CHECK-NEXT: Main.apply#[[N:[0-9]+]] (%{{[0-9]+}} : w Int) : Int =
CHECK-NEXT: let %{{[0-9]+}} : w Int = add_Int(10:Int, %{{[0-9]+}})
CHECK-NEXT: %{{[0-9]+}}
rule: CORE-OPT-1
First-order code is not inlined by the middle end; MLIR does that.
CHECK: -- specialization of Main.main() .PrimIO.MkIO#0 @(_:%World)
CHECK-NEXT: Main.main#{{[0-9]+}} (%{{[0-9]+}} : 1 %World)
CHECK-NEXT: Main.apply#[[N]](5:Int)
